{
  "statement_prompt": "Extract semantic facts, type declarations, inheritance relationships, rules, and negations.\n\nThe output is not PLN text. Return LangExtract objects with these extraction classes:\n- fact: a predicate with one or more arguments. Attributes: predicate, plus either arguments or subject/object.\n- type_decl: declares that an entity belongs to a type. Attributes: entity, type.\n- property: assigns a property value to an entity. Attributes: entity, property, value.\n- inheritance: subtype or kind-of relationship. Attributes: child, parent.\n- rule: a conditional implication. Attributes: head_predicate, head_args, body.\n- negation: explicit negation of a unary or binary fact. Attributes: predicate, plus either arguments or subject/object.\n\nRules:\n- Use lowercase hyphen-separated predicate names, such as eats-fish or can-fly.\n- Entity and type names may preserve source casing.\n- Hyphens and digits inside source identifiers are preserved, such as Object-77 and Rack-01.\n- Variables in rules must start with $, such as $x.\n- rule.head_args must be a space-separated argument string.\n- rule.body must be a valid S-expression using the same predicate names.\n- Use (and ...) for multi-premise rule bodies.\n- Definitional sentences become rules with a single-atom body.\n- Emit each causal/transitive link as a separate rule.\n- Use exact source spans for extraction_text; do not paraphrase.",
  "query_prompt": "Extract one or more executable logical queries from the question.\n\nReturn LangExtract objects with extraction_class=query.\nAttributes:\n- predicate: lowercase hyphen-separated predicate name.\n- arguments: ordered argument list.\n\nRules:\n- Yes/no questions should use grounded arguments from the question.\n- Who/what/which questions should use variables such as $who, $what, or $x.\n- \"is a kind of\", \"is a\", and type/class questions should use predicate=isa.\n- Property questions may use predicate=has with arguments [entity, property, value].\n- Reuse predicate names from the provided context when possible.\n- Do not output PLN syntax directly.",
